@startuml
title SIC/XE Parser and Lexical Helpers — Implementation Structure
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "Assembler::Engine (caller)" {
  class "Engine::run / source scan" as Engine
  class "parseLine(text, lineNo, diagnostics)" as ParseLine
  Engine --> ParseLine : one physical line at a time
}

package "parser.cpp — anonymous namespace" {
  class "Line parser" as ParseImpl {
    parseLine(text, lineNo, diagnostics)
    first-field operation/label decision
    modifier parsing and ISA resolution
  }
  class "Line field scanner" as FieldScanner {
    nextField(start)
    whitespace-delimited string_view
  }
  class "Operand field splitter" as OperandSplitter {
    splitOperands(text, baseCol)
    quote-aware comma split
    trim and preserve source columns
  }
  class "Mnemonic normalization" as MnemonicNorm {
    toUpper(text)
    operationMnemonic(text)
  }
  class "Comment stripping" as CommentStrip {
    stripComment(line)
    apostrophe quote tracking
  }
  class "Character predicates" as CharPredicates {
    isSpace(char)
    isIdentifier(text)
  }
  class "Instruction operand dispatcher" as InstParser {
    parseInstructionOperands(ctx)
    switch on OperandSchema
  }
  class "Directive operand dispatcher" as DirParser {
    parseDirectiveOperands(ctx)
    switch on DirectiveKind
  }
  class "Memory operand parser" as MemoryParser {
    parseMemoryOperand(ctx)
    # / @ prefix, optional index
  }
  class "Register parser" as RegisterParser {
    parseRegister(ctx, field)
    require '$' prefix
  }
  class "Literal decoder" as LiteralParser {
    parseLiteral(ctx, field, bytes)
    C literal / X literal
  }
  class "Expression boundary" as ExprBoundary {
    parseExprField(ctx, field)
    delegates to parseExpression
  }
  class "Error helper" as ErrorHelpers {
    fail(ctx, col, message)
    arity(ctx, min, max)
  }
  class "Register alias selector" as AliasSelector {
    looksLikeRegisterOperand(field)
    registerFormAlias(mnemonic)
  }
}

package "Assembler model / shared services" {
  class Statement {
    line, source
    label, labelCol
    mnemonic, mnemonicCol, operandCol
    extended, relativeMode
    instruction or directive identity
    mode, indexed
    expr, reg1, reg2, items
    valid
  }
  class "Field" as Field {
    text : string
    col : int
  }
  class "Diagnostics" as Diagnostics
  class "InstructionDef" as InstructionDef {
    schema : OperandSchema
  }
  class "DataItem" as DataItem {
    isLiteral
    literal bytes or expression
  }
  class "ISA catalog" as ISA {
    findInstruction
    findDirective
    registerNumber
  }
  class "Expression parser" as ExprParser
}

ParseLine --> ParseImpl : delegates
ParseImpl ..> CommentStrip : remove semicolon comment
ParseImpl ..> FieldScanner : scan whitespace fields
ParseImpl ..> MnemonicNorm : normalize / peel modifiers
ParseImpl ..> CharPredicates : whitespace and label checks
ParseImpl ..> OpcodeLookup : classify first field + resolve operation
ParseImpl ..> OperandSplitter : preserve comma-separated operands
ParseImpl ..> AliasSelector : inspect register-form aliases
ParseImpl ..> InstParser : dispatch by instruction schema
ParseImpl ..> DirParser : dispatch by directive kind
ParseImpl ..> ErrorHelpers : report diagnostic and invalidate

CommentStrip ..> CharPredicates
FieldScanner ..> CharPredicates
OperandSplitter ..> CharPredicates : trim fields
OpcodeLookup --> ISA
AliasSelector --> ISA : registerNumber / lookup alias
InstParser --> InstructionDef : schema switch
InstParser ..> MemoryParser : Memory schema
InstParser ..> RegisterParser : Reg / RegReg / RegCount
InstParser ..> ExprBoundary : numeric expression fields
DirParser ..> LiteralParser : BYTE / WORD literal candidates
DirParser ..> ExprBoundary : expression items
MemoryParser ..> RegisterParser : optional index field
MemoryParser ..> ExprBoundary : address expression
RegisterParser --> ISA : registerNumber
LiteralParser ..> ErrorHelpers : malformed / odd-length / bad hex
ExprBoundary --> ExprParser : expression text + line + source column

ParseImpl --> Statement : returns Statement
OperandSplitter --> Field : list of (text, start column)
InstParser --> Statement : mode, registers, expr, indexed
DirParser --> Statement : expr or DataItem vector
DirParser --> DataItem
ErrorHelpers --> Diagnostics : error(line, column, message)
ErrorHelpers --> Statement : valid = false
ParseImpl --> Diagnostics : line-level errors

note right of ParseImpl
There is no standalone Lexer class or token stream.
Lexical work is performed by local helpers in parser.cpp:
line comments, whitespace fields, comma splitting,
quote tracking, normalization, and identifier checks.
The parser consumes string_views and creates Field records
only for comma-separated operand pieces.
end note

note bottom of Statement
Parsing records syntax and source locations only.
Address, size, bytes, and pass validity are filled later
by the assembler passes.
end note
@enduml
